#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Fake codex for coder-codex.js: an interactive session the way codex 0.172.0
# keeps one, without a model. It mints its own session id, writes the rollout
# under $CODEX_HOME/sessions/<y>/<m>/<d>/rollout-<time>-<id>.jsonl with the
# first message and never before, holds that file open from then on, keeps
# names in session_index.jsonl, and answers `resume`, `delete --force`, the
# `thread/start`, `thread/name/set`, `thread/resume` and `thread/compact/start`
# calls of `app-server` over stdio (see compact_thread) and `debug models`
# with a catalog of codex's shape: two listed models and a hidden one.
# `exec resume --json` is one turn of an assistant, see turn().
#
# The pane says what the cockpit has to pin: ARGV (the arguments as JSON),
# CWD, TRUST (whether the -c projects override trusts the working directory),
# MODE (yolo with --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox, else ask),
# COLORS (TERM and COLORTERM, unset when absent), THEME (the syntax theme
# of the -c tui.theme override, none without one) and BELL (on with the three
# -c tui.notification overrides that make codex ring the plain bell on every
# turn end and question, else off).
#
# A line typed into it is a message, and a message is a turn in the rollout
# the way codex records one: task_started, the user's words and the answer as
# item_completed events beside the response items the model was sent, then
# task_complete, and with BELL on the bell. /rename <name> writes the
# session's record like codex does, also before the first message, and names
# it, BG asks the terminal for its background the way codex does at its start
# and says BACKGROUND with the answer, without writing a record. ASK records
# a tool call, and in ask mode rings, asks `Allow command? (y/n)` and answers
# APPROVED or DENIED once the call has its output. WORK says WORKING and keeps
# its turn open inside a tool call, painting and setting the terminal's title
# like codex's spinner does, until Enter ends it with FINISHED or Escape
# aborts it with INTERRUPTED (turn_aborted, no bell). LS lists the working
# directory, HOME what codex's home holds (HOMEFILES, no record), FORGET drops
# the session's own record, every other line is answered with ANSWER pong.
